cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite both the software and the dataset."
title: "quantum-pde-solvers: quantum linear solvers for the Poisson equation and Hall-effect thruster electrostatics"
abstract: >-
  A computational framework benchmarking three quantum linear system algorithms
  — HHL, VQLS and QSVT — against the classical Thomas algorithm, on the Poisson
  equation in one, two and three dimensions and on a Hall-effect thruster
  (SPT-100) electrostatics model. Two and three dimensions are decomposed into
  one-dimensional strips solved by an outer classical iteration, which bounds the
  condition number each quantum solve sees.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Trobajo Flecha"
    given-names: "Juan"
    affiliation: "Department of Aeronautics, Imperial College London"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jatf-gt/quantum-pde-solvers"
# MIT covers this repository's own code; see LICENSE. The dataset deposit
# referenced below stays CC-BY-4.0, which is the right licence for data and the
# wrong one for software. The submodule `quantum_linear_solvers/` is a separate
# repository under Apache-2.0 and keeps its own terms.
#
# No licence can compel an academic citation. MIT requires only that the
# copyright notice travel with the code; the citation is a request, and this
# file is where it is made.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum linear systems
  - HHL
  - variational quantum linear solver
  - quantum singular value transformation
  - Poisson equation
  - Hall-effect thruster
  - plasma electrostatics
  - Qiskit
references:
  - type: data
    title: >-
      Per-solution field archives for quantum linear-solver benchmarks on the
      Poisson equation and Hall-effect thruster electrostatics
    authors:
